From d04517bf722b7dc518ea142455cb002e31a0d271 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:59:44 +0100
Subject: [RFC PATCH 5/7] KVM: s390: Report a refused ESA/390-format state
 description without a warning

A machine or a hypervisor below KVM that does not run state descriptions
without the z/Architecture flag answers SIE with a validity interception.
A KVM below this one does that with reason code 0x0001 unless its user
space enabled KVM_CAP_S390_VSIE_ESAMODE. Once user space can put a VM into
the ESA/390-compatibility mode, it can reach this case on such a host, and
handle_validity() would print a WARN with a backtrace for something that is
neither a defect of KVM nor of the guest.

For reason code 0x0001 while the configuration is in the mode, print a
rate-limited message that names the cause instead and fail KVM_RUN with
-EINVAL as before. Every other validity interception keeps the warning.

The refusal cannot be detected before SIE is entered: no facility or SCLP
indication tells whether the levels below run such state descriptions.

No functional change as long as no vCPU is in the mode.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/s390/kvm/s390/intercept.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/s390/kvm/s390/intercept.c b/arch/s390/kvm/s390/intercept.c
index a87aeb3af0fa..038d2b4ca197 100644
--- a/arch/s390/kvm/s390/intercept.c
+++ b/arch/s390/kvm/s390/intercept.c
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
  *               Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@de.ibm.com>
  */
 
+#define pr_fmt(fmt) "kvm-s390: " fmt
+
 #include <linux/kvm_host.h>
 #include <linux/errno.h>
 #include <linux/pagemap.h>
@@ -98,6 +100,18 @@ static int handle_validity(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu)
 	KVM_EVENT(3, "validity intercept 0x%x for pid %u (kvm 0x%p)", viwhy,
 		  current->pid, vcpu->kvm);
 
+	/*
+	 * A machine or hypervisor that does not run state descriptions in the
+	 * ESA/390 format refuses them with reason code 0x0001. User space
+	 * asked for the ESA/390-compatibility mode: report it, but do not
+	 * treat it as a defect of KVM.
+	 */
+	if (viwhy == 0x0001 && kvm_s390_vcpu_is_esa(vcpu)) {
+		pr_warn_ratelimited("ESA/390-compatibility mode not available, validity intercept 0x1 for pid %d\n",
+				    current->pid);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	/* do not warn on invalid runtime instrumentation mode */
 	WARN_ONCE(viwhy != 0x44, "kvm: unhandled validity intercept 0x%x\n",
 		  viwhy);
-- 
